  "description": "The 2026 Oklahoma gubernatorial election is an open-seat race to elect the next governor of Oklahoma. Incumbent Republican Governor Kevin Stitt is term-limited and cannot seek a third term. Oklahoma is a deeply red state where Democrats have not won a statewide race since 2006, and the Republican primary is widely viewed as the most competitive contest for the office. The Republican field features four leading candidates — Attorney General Gentner Drummond, former state senator Mike Mazzei (endorsed by Donald Trump), former House Speaker Charles McCall, and former Secretary of Public Safety Chip Keating — while the Democratic primary includes House Minority Leader Cyndi Munson, former state senator Connie Johnson, and securities trader Arya Azma. The primary election is scheduled for June 16, 2026, and the general election will be held on November 3, 2026.",
